 $329), which is under the $2,500 approval threshold. Placing it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KLJN4jPtJPPQfmsU2B3Y1C", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "new-hire-dk200-mn27-hq-2024-001"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so I can't tell whether it committed. I'll check the existing orders before retrying so I don't create a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SzXQ4gtPvYUvzsN2zVidsn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The timeout left a partial order (PO0001) with only the 3 docks committed, and the monitors are missing. Following the recovery procedure, I'll undo the partial commit using the same key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WjWghXLotSUiNxHsehCfnW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"tool": "place_order", "key": "new-hire-dk200-mn27-hq-2024-001"}, "name": "cancel_partial", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The partial commit has been undone (the $567 charge was reversed). Resending the full order with the same key.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_0156MGzXdow4Edk4faAorYbH", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "new-hire-dk200-mn27-hq-2024-001"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015wikJQ9zsRJz38Fs7F3cRD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I placed the order as a single purchase order, PO0002, for shipment to HQ. It totals $1,554:\n\n- 3 \u00d7 DK-200 USB-C Dock (new, $189 each = $567)\n- 3 \u00d7 MN-27 27-inch 4K Monitor (new, $329 each = $987)\n\nThe DK-200 was in stock, so I didn't use the DK-210 fallback. The order is under the $2,500 threshold, so no manager approval was needed.\n\nThe first attempt timed out and left a partial order (PO0001) with only the docks charged ($567). I reversed that partial charge using the same idempotency key, then resent the full order under that key. PO0001 now shows as cancelled, and the account carries only the $1,554 charge for PO0002.", "type": "text"}]}]}